# Picodroid bench fleet: one row per board slot. Copy to
# ~/.config/picodroid/fleet.conf (or point PICODROID_FLEET_CONF at it).
# Without this file every script assumes one board on the bench, as before.
#
#   slot|probe_serial|board_usb_path|boards[|extras]
#
#   slot            the lease name; device-lock.sh --slot NAME
#   probe_serial    USB serial of this slot's Debug Probe (`probe-rs list`,
#                   or ./scripts/fleet.sh discover)
#   board_usb_path  sysfs position of the board's own USB port (its pdb CDC
#                   device), e.g. 1-8.3.3 -- the device has no serial string,
#                   so the physical port is its identity
#   boards          comma list of firmware boards this hardware accepts.
#                   The FIRST is what hil-fleet.sh flashes for ordinary rows;
#                   the rest let `flash.sh -b X` and net rows route here
#                   (a Pico 2 W with the Enviro+ pack runs pico_enviro_mon_w,
#                   testbench_rp2350w and plain testbench_rp2350 firmware).
#   extras          optional key=value list:
#                     probe_path=1-8.3.2  the probe's sysfs position, so it can
#                                         be power-cycled back on even when it
#                                         is off (recommended)
#                     cycle=hub           power-cycle the whole hub instead of
#                                         the two ports (use when each board
#                                         has its own hub, or the hub switches
#                                         all ports together)
#
# `./scripts/fleet.sh discover` prints the probes and boards it can see with
# these positions; `./scripts/fleet.sh check` validates this file.
testbench_rp2350|E6633861A35F8938|1-8.3.3|testbench_rp2350|probe_path=1-8.3.2
pico_enviro_mon_w|E66XXXXXXXXXXXXX|1-8.3.4|pico_enviro_mon_w,testbench_rp2350w,testbench_rp2350|probe_path=1-8.3.1
